# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# Every terminal golden under tests/snapshots and tests/replay is compared
# BYTE-for-byte against a rendered frame, and the recorded session fixture is
# parsed line by line. A Windows checkout with the default `core.autocrlf=true`
# would rewrite all of them to CRLF, and the whole snapshot suite would fail on
# Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with talon's rendering — which is
# exactly the "Windows 快照稳定" acceptance line (spec §8 T4).
#
# So: everything textual is normalized to LF in the repository AND checked out
# as LF on every platform. `tests/windows.spec.ts` asserts the result, so a file
# that slips through fails loudly instead of only on someone else's machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the two families the snapshots actually depend on.
*.expected.txt text eol=lf
*.jsonl        text eol=lf
